To implement the server-side filtering while keeping your existing logic intact, we need to modify the method to accept page, size, batchId, and vid. We will convert the List<Map<String, Object>> return type to a Map<String, Object> so you can return the content (the rows) and the totalElements (for pagination).
### 1. The Controller Change
Update your controller to accept the new request parameters:
```java
@GetMapping("/checker/pending-approvals")
public ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>> getPendingApprovals(
        @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token,
        @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") int page,
        @RequestParam(defaultValue = "10") int size,
        @RequestParam(required = false, defaultValue = "") String batchId,
        @RequestParam(required = false, defaultValue = "") String vid) {
    
    Integer userRole = jwtUtil.getUserRoleFromToken(token);
